Here's how to create a custom filter in Spring Cloud Gateway (WebFlux) that reads the session, request URI, and remote IP address:

## Custom Global Filter Implementation

```java
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.filter.GatewayFilterChain;
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.filter.GlobalFilter;
import org.springframework.core.Ordered;
import org.springframework.http.server.reactive.ServerHttpRequest;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import org.springframework.web.server.ServerWebExchange;
import org.springframework.web.server.WebSession;
import reactor.core.publisher.Mono;

import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.net.URI;

@Component
public class CustomSessionFilter implements GlobalFilter, Ordered {

    @Override
    public Mono<Void> filter(ServerWebExchange exchange, GatewayFilterChain chain) {
        return exchange.getSession().flatMap(session -> {
            // Get the session
            WebSession webSession = session;
            
            // Get the request
            ServerHttpRequest request = exchange.getRequest();
            
            // Get the request URI
            URI requestUri = request.getURI();
            
            // Get the remote IP address
            InetSocketAddress remoteAddress = request.getRemoteAddress();
            String remoteIp = remoteAddress != null ? remoteAddress.getAddress().getHostAddress() : "unknown";
            
            // Log or process the data
            System.out.println("Session ID: " + webSession.getId());
            System.out.println("Request URI: " + requestUri);
            System.out.println("Remote IP: " + remoteIp);
            System.out.println("Request Path: " + request.getPath());
            
            // You can also get session attributes
            Object userId = webSession.getAttribute("userId");
            if (userId != null) {
                System.out.println("User ID from session: " + userId);
            }
            
            // Continue the filter chain
            return chain.filter(exchange);
        });
    }

    @Override
    public int getOrder() {
        return -1; // Execute early in the filter chain
    }
}
```

## Alternative: Custom GatewayFilter Factory

If you want more control over which routes use this filter:

```java
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.filter.GatewayFilter;
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.filter.factory.AbstractGatewayFilterFactory;
import org.springframework.http.server.reactive.ServerHttpRequest;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import org.springframework.web.server.WebSession;

import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.net.URI;

@Component
public class CustomSessionGatewayFilterFactory 
        extends AbstractGatewayFilterFactory<CustomSessionGatewayFilterFactory.Config> {

    public CustomSessionGatewayFilterFactory() {
        super(Config.class);
    }

    @Override
    public GatewayFilter apply(Config config) {
        return (exchange, chain) -> {
            return exchange.getSession().flatMap(session -> {
                ServerHttpRequest request = exchange.getRequest();
                URI requestUri = request.getURI();
                InetSocketAddress remoteAddress = request.getRemoteAddress();
                String remoteIp = remoteAddress != null 
                    ? remoteAddress.getAddress().getHostAddress() 
                    : "unknown";

                // Store in session if needed
                if (config.isStoreIp()) {
                    session.getAttributes().put("remoteIp", remoteIp);
                }

                System.out.println("Session ID: " + session.getId());
                System.out.println("URI: " + requestUri);
                System.out.println("Remote IP: " + remoteIp);

                return chain.filter(exchange);
            });
        };
    }

    public static class Config {
        private boolean storeIp = false;

        public boolean isStoreIp() {
            return storeIp;
        }

        public void setStoreIp(boolean storeIp) {
            this.storeIp = storeIp;
        }
    }
}
```

## Configuration in application.yml

```yaml
spring:
  cloud:
    gateway:
      routes:
        - id: my-route
          uri: http://localhost:8080
          predicates:
            - Path=/api/**
          filters:
            - CustomSession # If using GatewayFilterFactory
```

## Getting Real IP Behind Proxy

If you're behind a load balancer or proxy:

```java
import org.springframework.http.HttpHeaders;

// Inside your filter method
private String getRealIp(ServerHttpRequest request) {
    // Check X-Forwarded-For header first
    String ip = request.getHeaders().getFirst("X-Forwarded-For");
    
    if (ip == null || ip.isEmpty() || "unknown".equalsIgnoreCase(ip)) {
        ip = request.getHeaders().getFirst("X-Real-IP");
    }
    
    if (ip == null || ip.isEmpty() || "unknown".equalsIgnoreCase(ip)) {
        InetSocketAddress remoteAddress = request.getRemoteAddress();
        ip = remoteAddress != null 
            ? remoteAddress.getAddress().getHostAddress() 
            : "unknown";
    }
    
    // X-Forwarded-For can contain multiple IPs, get the first one
    if (ip != null && ip.contains(",")) {
        ip = ip.split(",")[0].trim();
    }
    
    return ip;
}
```

## Session Configuration

Add session dependency in `pom.xml`:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.session</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-session-data-redis</artifactId>
</dependency>
```

And configure in `application.yml`:

```yaml
spring:
  session:
    store-type: redis
  redis:
    host: localhost
    port: 6379
```

## Key Points

* **GlobalFilter** - Applies to all routes automatically
* **GatewayFilterFactory** - Applied selectively per route
* **Reactive** - Use `Mono` and `flatMap` for session access
* **Order** - Lower values execute first (use `Ordered` interface)
* **Session** - Requires Spring Session if you need distributed sessions

This filter will intercept all requests and log/process the session, URI, and IP address before forwarding to the downstream service.

